<Routines>
<Routine Name="ClearBuffer" Type="RLL">
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[ACL(0,Yes,Yes);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
<Routine Name="CRCLoopR" Type="RLL">
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XOR(uchCRCHi,Receive_Buffer[uLoop],uIndex)XOR(uchCRCLo,uchaCRCHi[uIndex],uchCRCHi);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[MOV(uchaCRCLo[uIndex],uchCRCLo);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
<Routine Name="CRCLoopT" Type="RLL">
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XOR(uchCRCHi,Trans_Buffer[uLoop],uIndex)XOR(uchCRCLo,uchaCRCHi[uIndex],uchCRCHi);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[MOV(uchaCRCLo[uIndex],uchCRCLo);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
<Routine Name="DataPack" Type="RLL">
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[LBL(Swap)GEQ(LCounter2,Quantity)RET();]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(ReadHReg)SWPB(Mod_Data_HoldReg4[LCounter1],REVERSE,DataHold[LCounter2]);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(ReadIRegisters)SWPB(Mod_Data_InpReg3[LCounter1],REVERSE,DataHold[LCounter2]);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[ADD(LCounter1,1,LCounter1)ADD(LCounter2,1,LCounter2)JMP(Swap);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
<Routine Name="MainRoutine" Type="RLL">
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[
All information provided  - No Warranty or implied merchantability. 
Refer to the RSLogix 5000 End User License Agreement (EULA) in the Release Notes.

]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[NOP();]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[
********************************
Revision History
********************************
Release 1.0 initial release
********************************
Release 2.0.0 Modified by Commercial Engineering

Modified multiple rungs that caused arithmetic overflow minor faults, no functional change.
Improved documentation.
Modifications to allow for addressing of Coils and Registers up to 65,535. This change also increased the size of the program from about 49K to 327K. This size can be reduced if you only need to read a smaller number of Coils and Registers.
Renamed tag array Mod_DataHoldReg4 to Mod_Data_HoldReg4, no functional change.
Renamed tag array Mod_RangeHoldReg4 to Mod_Range_HoldReg4, no functional change.
Renamed tag array Mod_Range_Cont1 to Mod_Range_Contacts1, no functional change.
Modified serial port User Protocol Read/Write buffer size from 140 to 280 characters.
Increased range of reads and writes to cover documented values of 1-2000 bit and 1-120 register.
Resolved multiple issues with bit reads and writes.
Removed input modules from I/O tree, no functional change.
********************************]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[NOP();]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Mod_Active)XIO(initial)JSR(ClearBuffer,0)OTL(initial);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Mod_Active)JSR(SlaveRecMonitor,0);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="4" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Mod_Active)OTU(initial);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
