<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(ReadHReg) ,XIC(ReadIRegisters) ]MOV(0,LCounter2)MOV(Addr,LCounter1);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="40" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(WriteCoils)XIC(WordBoundary)SUB(WordCount2,1,WordCount2)COP(Receive_Buffer[7],Mod_Data_Coils0[WordStartC],WordCount2);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="41" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(WriteCoils)XIO(WordBoundary)JSR(WriteCoils,0);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="42" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[This rung does a read/modify/write of Coils0 back to itself only manipulating one bit at a time. Bit 15 is not done through the OR because if using an OR with an indirectly addressed Dest, if the Dest ends up negative after the OR is executed an arithmetic overflow will occur and cause a minor fault.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(WriteOneCoil)NEQ(Receive_Buffer[4],0)[XIC(Mod_Data_Coils0[WordStartC].15) OTE(Bit15_Store_OR) OTU(Mod_Data_Coils0[WordStartC].15) ,OR(Mod_Data_Coils0[WordStartC],MaskOr[BitStartC],Mod_Data_Coils0[WordStartC]) ,[XIC(Bit15_Store_OR) ,EQU(BitStartC,15) ] OTL(Mod_Data_Coils0[WordStartC].15) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="43" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[This rung does a read/modify/write of Coils0 back to itself only manipulating one bit at a time. Bit 15 is not done through the AND because if using an AND with an indirectly addressed Dest, if the Dest ends up negative after the AND is executed an arithmetic overflow will occur and cause a minor fault.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(WriteOneCoil)EQU(Receive_Buffer[4],0)[XIC(Mod_Data_Coils0[WordStartC].15) OTE(Bit15_Store_AND) OTU(Mod_Data_Coils0[WordStartC].15) ,AND(Mod_Data_Coils0[WordStartC],MaskAnd[BitStartC],Mod_Data_Coils0[WordStartC]) ,[XIC(Bit15_Store_AND) OTL(Mod_Data_Coils0[WordStartC].15) ,EQU(BitStartC,15) OTU(Mod_Data_Coils0[WordStartC].15) ] ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
